I started off a little unsure how to approach the idea of consolidating the pieces of
my Kotlin code into a running program. Based on past languages we used, I assumed it
relied on a Main() type function.

I did my code review with Dylan, who pointed out that that wasn't the ideal way to approach
the code, especially in light of what would be required of us for Phase 2. As a result, I did
away with my Main() function entirely (as well as a handful of other supporting functions
that only existed to set up parameters for Main()) and moved towards a more UI-based approach.